  "question": {
    "text": "A $10 \\mathrm{~kW}$ transmitter emits radio waves of wavelength $500 \\mathrm{~m}$. The number of photons emitted per second by the transmitter is of the order of",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AE3C1",
      "text": "\n$10^{37}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QZAZN",
      "text": "\n$10^{31}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "4usPZ",
      "text": "\n$10^{25}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ovVOs",
      "text": "\n$10^{43}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Power $=\\frac{n h c}{\\lambda}$\n(where, $n=$ no. of photons per second)\n$$\n\\Rightarrow \\quad n=\\frac{10 \\times 10^3 \\times 500}{6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\times 3 \\times 10^8} \\simeq 10^{31}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
